    "body": "Hands-on GUI check by the contributor (macOS, this branch's release build, 2026-11-09). The test project was a 2\" x 1\" x 0.5\" block. Setup1 holds it as modelled, with its WCS on the back-right top corner (50.8, 25.4, 12.7). Setup2 flips it over X.\n\n- **Setup2 active:** Setup1's triad sits on the flipped block's front-right **bottom** corner (50.8, 0, 0), with Z pointing down. Both the position and the orientation follow the part.\n- **Setup1 active:** the triad is back on the top corner.\n- **Switching back and forth:** it stays on the same physical corner every time.\n\nThis closes the review's non-blocking 'nobody has looked at a flipped part in the real GUI yet'.",
